      "body": "Decision record for #5833 — decomposition item 4 of #5677 (edit/fork graph). Queue task 14114.\n\n## What this settles\n\n- **Graph model**: the edit/fork graph is a projection over the landed signed revision DAG (#3814, `pkgs/id/src/notes.rs`). A **lineage** — a maximal unbranched path identified by its first revision — partitions the DAG deterministically; forks are first-class citizens that get **no new object identity**.\n- **Divergence views**: deterministic projections comparing lineages by ancestry set-difference (well-defined under criss-cross merges); every lineage disclosed, none hidden by demotion or rejection; default-lineage selection is a view default, never a gate.\n- **Mark-most-correct**: attributed, scoped, superseding marks recorded in the object's changelog — one current mark per (object, community scope), set by the owner of record or a scope admin, following the lineage as it extends, always displayed scope-qualified. This is the marking mechanism the ranking record (#5836 §7) defers to this design; §5 rule 7 states the consumer mapping (tier 2 = marked lineage's current tip) and that mark semantics impose no cross-signal precedence, so #5836 §9's default stands unamended.\n- **Merge proposals**: recorded coordination objects (open → merged / rejected / withdrawn / superseded) around the substrate's explicit signed merge revision; rejection never deletes the rejected line; proposals are a gate only where #5835 approval governance requires them.\n\n## Boundaries kept\n\nParent-fixed decisions (note↔board reference model, session merge model, sovereignty rule, approval flow shape) are cited, not re-decided; §8 states the boundary with each sibling (#5830, #5831, #5832, #5834, #5835, #5836) and the substrate. Implementation slices (§9) wait on the #5834 changelog model and are filed when it lands, per the record.\n\nVerified at origin/main `aa01b61853`: the revision DAG exists as described; no fork-graph/mark/proposal record existed (`git grep` for mark-most-correct over `doc/` and `pkgs/id/src` empty before this PR).\n\nDocs-only change; no code touched.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796788864&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7943&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7943&signature=7a5929cc597058f6a09504f988d5c8470e1a6d4d818267b4a2b1a19fa1a7bac8\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7943?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
