      "body": "Implements #3846 (F13.8 Phase 2, parent #790). Queue task 5833.\n\n## What\n\nDocuments and regression-tests the client-only authority boundary:\n\n- **CLI help** — the `World` command doc now states every `world` subcommand is a client command: it connects out to a host, opening further world sessions starts no listener/host/authority, there is no `--client-only` flag because no world subcommand has a server mode, and node connectivity is not world authority (a valid world capability is still required). The `Serve` doc names `id serve` as the only command that starts a server or listener, with SSH world serving opt-in via its flags.\n- **README** — a new \"Client-only boundary\" section plus a pointer in the usage examples.\n- **Regression test** — `test_world_client_commands_never_dispatch_serve` in `cli.rs`: representative client argvs (`world join`, `invite`, `records`, `list`) parse to `Command::World`, never `Command::Serve` (the only arm `main` dispatches server startup from); `id serve` still parses as `Serve`; `--client-only` is rejected.\n\n## Scope\n\nDocs + one parse-level test only. No runtime behaviour, hosting, or capability changes; no redundant `--client-only` flag (per #3846's exclusion). The concurrent multi-server coordinator stays with #3845.\n\nDocs/test-only diff (78 insertions, 2 files). Tests run in CI per the fleet's CI-first rule.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/3862?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796144973&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=3862&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F3862&signature=02fc34d0060162e2620aa58cfee8f2485210da723a2c910123cd8aae0faad230\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
